{"id":"sponsor-organizations","title":"Organizations that hold money for other projects","question":"Which City-paid organizations say on their own tax returns that they act as fiscal sponsor for other groups, how much has the City paid them, and what do the returns show of the fee?","finding":"28 City-paid organizations say on their own returns that they sponsor other projects; the City paid them $552.1 million from fiscal 2019 to 2027 to date, led by Heluna Health ($165.5 million); Tides Center ($106.7 million); San Francisco Public Health Foundation ($72.7 million); Richmond District Neighborhood Ctr Inc ($28.3 million). Only 9 of the 28 show the fee as a line of its own: Northern California Grantmakers ($410,444, 6.7% of its revenue); Dancers' Group ($302,887, 7.0% of its revenue); Z Space Studio ($215,892, 9.1% of its revenue); New Community Leadership Foundation ($150,000, 8.9% of its revenue). For the rest the fee is inside a general line such as service fees, so the share kept cannot be read from the return. 8 of the 28 are also among the large onward grant-makers listed in the grant-chains file; 1 more organization says it was itself a sponsored project, and 9 show only an expense line with the words.","how":"Every return on file (tax years 2020 to 2025, latest version of each) was searched for the words “fiscal sponsor” or “fiscally sponsored” in its mission statement, programme descriptions, supplemental notes, schedule notes, expense lines and revenue lines. An organization is counted as saying it sponsors others when the words describe its own activity (“is the fiscal sponsor for”, “provides fiscal sponsorship”, “its fiscally sponsored projects”) or label a revenue line. Fee income is the revenue line carrying those words in the latest return that has one, read from the return’s own file; its share is of total revenue that year. City money is everything the payment file shows under the organization’s names, leaving out money the City only collects and passes through (benefit-district assessments).","limits":"Fiscal sponsorship is common: a registered charity lets a project that has no tax-exempt status of its own operate under the charity’s, keeps its books and charges a fee; the returns read here describe it in those terms. A sponsor’s City money is mostly for programmes it runs itself, so the total here is not money passed on. Assessments the City collects for benefit districts and hands back are left out of City money throughout. A return need not mention sponsorship at all, so the list is a floor; and a phrase about “fiscal sponsorship” can describe a small side activity. An expense line with the words may be a fee the organization pays to its own sponsor, or money it pays out for projects it sponsors: the label alone does not say which. What would settle the share kept: each sponsor’s sponsorship agreement and fee schedule, and for a City grant paid through a sponsor, the grant budget’s indirect-cost line.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Organization","type":"org"},{"k":"says","t":"What its return says","type":"text"},{"k":"where","t":"Where the words appear","type":"text"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City paid it, fiscal 2019–2027","type":"usd"},{"k":"yearEnd","t":"Latest return, year ended","type":"date"},{"k":"revenue","t":"Total revenue","type":"usd"},{"k":"feeIncome","t":"Income on a line labelled fiscal sponsorship","type":"usd"},{"k":"feeLabel","t":"That line’s label","type":"text"},{"k":"feeShare","t":"As a share of revenue","type":"pct"},{"k":"expenseLine","t":"Expense lines with the words","type":"usd"},{"k":"expenseLabel","t":"Their labels","type":"text"},{"k":"grantsOut","t":"Grants it paid to organizations","type":"usd"},{"k":"regranter","t":"In the grant-chains list of large onward grant-makers","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"org":"Heluna Health","orgKey":"HELUNA HEALTH","says":"it sponsors other projects","where":"supplemental notes (Schedule O)","cityPaid":165525415,"yearEnd":"2025-06-30","revenue":686293901,"feeIncome":null,"feeShare":null,"feeLabel":"","expenseLine":null,"expenseLabel":"","grantsOut":null,"regranter":""},{"org":"Tides Center","orgKey":"TIDES CENTER","says":"it sponsors other projects","where":"mission statement; notes to the financial schedules (Schedule D)","cityPaid":106727388,"yearEnd":"2024-12-31","revenue":265402095,"feeIncome":null,"feeShare":null,"feeLabel":"","expenseLine":null,"expenseLabel":"","grantsOut":49629831,"regranter":"yes"},{"org":"San Francisco Public Health Foundation","orgKey":"SAN FRANCISCO PUBLIC HEALTH FOUNDATION","says":"it sponsors other projects","where":"supplemental notes (Schedule O)","cityPaid":72651672,"yearEnd":"2025-06-30","revenue":10273211,"feeIncome":null,"feeShare":null,"feeLabel":"","expenseLine":null,"expenseLabel":"","grantsOut":null,"regranter":""},{"org":"Richmond District Neighborhood Ctr Inc","orgKey":"RICHMOND DISTRICT NEIGHBORHOOD CENTER","says":"it sponsors other projects","where":"supplemental notes (Schedule O)","cityPaid":28287061,"yearEnd":"2025-06-30","revenue":12410041,"feeIncome":null,"feeShare":null,"feeLabel":"","expenseLine":null,"expenseLabel":"","grantsOut":123750,"regranter":""},{"org":"Centers For Equity And Success, Inc","orgKey":"CENTERS EQUITY SUCCESS","says":"it sponsors other projects","where":"supplemental notes (Schedule O)","cityPaid":27896097,"yearEnd":"2025-06-30","revenue":5431564,"feeIncome":7949,"feeShare":0.0015,"feeLabel":"Fiscal sponsorship fees","expenseLine":null,"expenseLabel":"","grantsOut":null,"regranter":""},{"org":"San Francisco Parks Alliance","orgKey":"SAN FRANCISCO PARKS ALLIANCE","says":"it sponsors other projects","where":"notes on grants made (Schedule I); supplemental notes (Schedule O)","cityPaid":19782241,"yearEnd":"2024-06-30","revenue":8141531,"feeIncome":null,"feeShare":null,"feeLabel":"","expenseLine":null,"expenseLabel":"","grantsOut":93563,"regranter":"yes"},{"org":"Community Initiatives","orgKey":"COMMUNITY INITIATIVES","says":"it sp